cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Processing and Figure-Generation Scripts for Evaluating a Double-Spherical-Shell Shield for Shallow-Water Ocean-Bottom Seismic Noise Reduction"
version: "1.0"
date-released: 2026-07-23
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Li"
    given-names: "Yang"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-8764-0536"
    affiliation: "Tongji University"

    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21511732"
    repository-code: "https://github.com/Blackleeeee/ESS-OBS-Shield-Processing.git"

abstract: >-
  MATLAB, Python, and shell scripts for instrument-response provenance,
  continuous-to-daily and daily-to-hourly SAC segmentation, hourly power
  spectral density calculation, root-mean-square analysis, and reproduction
  of the principal figures used to evaluate a double-spherical-shell shield
  for reducing flow-induced noise in shallow-water ocean-bottom seismic
  observations.
keywords:
  - ocean-bottom seismometer
  - shallow-water seismic observation
  - flow-induced noise
  - seismic noise reduction
  - power spectral density
  - root mean square
  - instrument response
  - MATLAB
  - ObsPy
  - shell script
